## H5: MFA and credential hygiene

```
Hypothesis H5: Administrators authenticate through a central service with MFA, accounts are individual, the built-in admin is not in active use, and lockout and idle timeout are set.

a. Under mgt-config/users: every account with its role and authentication-profile. Count superusers. Is an account named "admin" present, and is it bound to an authentication profile or local only?
b. Under shared/authentication-profile: method (local / radius / tacplus / ldap / saml / kerberos) and the server-profile it references.
c. MFA: any factor configured on-box? If the method is RADIUS or SAML, mark MFA NOT-DETERMINABLE; enforcement lives on the identity provider.
d. Accounts that look shared or generic (netadmin, service, ops, etc.).
e. Under deviceconfig/setting/management/admin-lockout: failed-attempts and lockout-time, or "lockout disabled" if absent.
f. Under deviceconfig/setting/management: idle-timeout, or "60-minute default" if absent.
g. Under mgt-config/password-complexity: enabled and minimum-length, or "not enforced" if absent.

Verdict: CONFIRMED only if central auth is in use, no shared accounts, lockout and idle timeout are set, and admin is not local-only. Report MFA separately as NOT-DETERMINABLE where applicable. Cite.
```

