## H6: Panorama enforces uniformly, no weakening overrides

```
Hypothesis H6: All management-plane settings are template-enforced with no local override that weakens them.

If the file does not indicate per-setting origin (local vs template), mark H6 NOT-DETERMINABLE and state that the comparison requires the running-config and template-config as separate inputs.

If it does: list every management-plane setting (permitted-ip, service disables, admin-lockout, idle-timeout, interface management profiles, admin accounts) whose origin is local rather than template. For any setting present in both with different values, state which value is effective (local) and whether it is more or less restrictive than the template value. Settings present in both with identical values are locked from Panorama management; note them as latent risk.

Verdict: CONFIRMED if no management-plane setting is locally configured or overridden with a weaker value. REFUTED otherwise. Cite.
```

